    "explain": [
      "These are the letters that look new. Some of them stand for sounds English writes with two letters (th, ps, ks): Greek has one letter for each.",
      {
        "letters": [
          {
            "letter": "Γ γ",
            "latin": "gh / y",
            "say": "a soft g made at the back of the throat; like the y in yes before e and i",
            "word": "γάλα",
            "word_latin": "ghála",
            "meaning": "milk"
          },
          {
            "letter": "Δ δ",
            "latin": "dh",
            "say": "like the th in this",
            "word": "δώρο",
            "word_latin": "dhóro",
            "meaning": "present"
          },
          {
            "letter": "Ζ ζ",
            "latin": "z",
            "say": "like the z in zoo",
            "word": "ζάχαρη",
            "word_latin": "záchari",
            "meaning": "sugar"
          },
          {
            "letter": "Θ θ",
